# Local + cloud test calls for the App Service connector-callback endpoint.
#
# The endpoint is  POST /api/onNewEmail  and it deserializes the body into the SDK's
# Office365OnNewEmailTriggerPayload — wire shape:
#     { "body": { "value": [ <GraphClientReceiveMessage>, ... ] } }
# (same shape the Functions [ConnectorTrigger] binding receives.)
#
# LOCAL (recommended for iterating on the pipeline):
#   1. az login                       (so DefaultAzureCredential can call the connections)
#   2. Populate .env from .env.sample  (connection runtime URLs + Teams IDs), or use
#      user-secrets / appsettings.Development.json.
#   3. dotnet run --project ./src      (listens on http://localhost:5280)
#   4. Send the requests below. There is NO Easy Auth locally, so no token is needed.
#
# CLOUD (https://<app>.azurewebsites.net):
#   Easy Auth guards every route. A raw POST with no token returns 401 — that is the
#   whole point of this sample. Only the Connector Namespace trigger (which attaches an
#   Entra token minted from the trigger UAMI) can call it. So the cloud "test" is to send
#   a real email to the connected mailbox, not to curl this endpoint. The unauthenticated
#   401 check below documents the security boundary.

@localUrl = http://localhost:5280
@appUrl = {{$dotenv APP_URL}}

### Liveness probe (local)
GET {{localUrl}}/healthz

### LOCAL — important email (allowlisted sender + urgent subject). Expect Teams card + flag.
POST {{localUrl}}/api/onNewEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": {
    "value": [
      {
        "id": "AAMkADlmOTA3NWNm",
        "receivedDateTime": "2026-03-25T10:30:00+00:00",
        "hasAttachments": false,
        "subject": "Urgent: action needed on connector demo",
        "bodyPreview": "Please review the connector demo before the summit session.",
        "importance": "high",
        "isRead": false,
        "isHtml": true,
        "body": "<html><body>Please review the connector demo before the summit. This is critical.</body></html>",
        "from": "important.sender@contoso.com",
        "toRecipients": "you@contoso.com"
      }
    ]
  }
}

### LOCAL — non-important email (normal newsletter). Expect: skipped, no Teams card.
POST {{localUrl}}/api/onNewEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": {
    "value": [
      {
        "id": "AAMkADlmOTA3NWNn",
        "receivedDateTime": "2026-03-25T11:00:00+00:00",
        "hasAttachments": false,
        "subject": "Weekly newsletter",
        "bodyPreview": "Here are this week's top stories.",
        "importance": "normal",
        "isRead": false,
        "isHtml": true,
        "body": "<html><body>Here are this week's top stories.</body></html>",
        "from": "newsletter@contoso.com",
        "toRecipients": "you@contoso.com"
      }
    ]
  }
}

### LOCAL — empty batch. Expect: 200, "nothing to process" log.
POST {{localUrl}}/api/onNewEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": { "value": [] } }

### CLOUD — security boundary check. Expect: 401 Unauthorized (Easy Auth, no token).
GET {{appUrl}}/api/onNewEmail

### CLOUD — POST with no token. Expect: 401 Unauthorized (proves the endpoint is not open).
POST {{appUrl}}/api/onNewEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": { "value": [] } }
